md("---",
   "## Mode 2 -- ROI co-sim (`run --model hybrid --cosim`)",
   "",
   "Lock-stepping a whole large program from reset is too slow. Instead, the",
   "**hybrid** model lets QEMU fast-forward to a region of interest (ROI), hands",
   "off to the RTL, and the RTL measures the ROI. `--cosim` adds a cross-check:",
   "every *N* retired instructions inside the ROI the RTL drains a checkpoint,",
   "and a pure-QEMU oracle re-runs draining at the **same** retire counts. The",
   "first mismatching window brackets the divergence.",
   "",
   "Here the ROI is delimited by the `andes_sim_roi_begin()/end()` markers the",
   "fixture carries (`--trigger marker`); `--cosim-interval` sets *N*.")

code(
"!andes-sim run --model hybrid --trigger marker --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium \\\n"
"    --cosim --cosim-interval 500 tests/fixtures/rt_c_v_matmul.elf",
out=(
"[andes-sim] model=hybrid engine=vsim:ax45mpv_premium vlen=512 trigger=marker fixture=rt_c_v_matmul\n"
"[andes-sim] cosim: oracle leg (pure QEMU, 4 sample(s))\n"
"[cosim] PASS: 3 checkpoint(s) + final state match the QEMU oracle (interval 500, 1690 ROI retires)\n"
"PASS: --model hybrid --trigger marker (rt_c_v_matmul)"),
n=6)

md("`PASS` means all three in-ROI checkpoints plus the final drain matched the",
   "oracle. On a mismatch you would get, e.g.:",
   "",
   "```",
   "[state-diff] x12: ref=0x2a got=0x2b",
   "[cosim] FAIL: divergence in retires 1000..1500 after entry (500 insn window)",
   "        at retire ~1500: pc vsim=0x100a3c qemu=0x100a3c   (vec_madd+0x40)",
   "```",
   "",
   "...which says the bug is in the 500-instruction window ending at retire 1500.",
   "That is coarse. To narrow it automatically, add `--cosim-refine`.")

md("### `--cosim-refine`: narrow toward the instruction",
   "",
   "`--cosim-refine` keeps subdividing the bad window ~16x per pass -- re-running",
   "QEMU1 -> RTL with explicit checkpoint targets inside it, re-running the oracle",
   "at the RTL's achieved retire counts -- until the window reaches the RTL's halt",
   "slack (a handful of instructions). On a matching program (no divergence) it is",
   "a no-op and reports the same `PASS`:")

code(
"!andes-sim run --model hybrid --trigger marker --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium \\\n"
"    --cosim --cosim-refine --cosim-interval 500 tests/fixtures/rt_c_v_matmul.elf",
out=(
"[andes-sim] model=hybrid engine=vsim:ax45mpv_premium vlen=512 trigger=marker fixture=rt_c_v_matmul\n"
"[andes-sim] cosim: oracle leg (pure QEMU, 4 sample(s))\n"
"[cosim] PASS: 3 checkpoint(s) + final state match the QEMU oracle (interval 500, 1690 ROI retires)\n"
"PASS: --model hybrid --trigger marker (rt_c_v_matmul)"),
n=7)

md("On a **real** divergence, the refine passes converge the window like this",
   "(illustrative -- the matching fixtures here never diverge):",
   "",
   "```",
   "[andes-sim] cosim-refine pass 2: window (0, 1690], 16 probes",
   "[andes-sim] cosim-refine pass 3: window (845, 951], 13 probes",
   "[andes-sim] cosim-refine pass 4: window (936, 944], 1 probes",
   "[state-diff] x14: ref=0x deadbeee got=0xdeadbeef",
   "[cosim] FAIL: divergence in retires 936..944 after entry (8 insn window), narrowed",
   "        at retire ~944: pc vsim=0x100a3c qemu=0x100a3c   (vec_madd+0x40)",
   "```",
   "",
   "Two refine passes took a 1690-instruction ROI down to an 8-instruction",
   "bracket around `vec_madd+0x40`, with the diverging register (`x14`) named.",
   "",
   "**Cost & limits (ROI cosim):**",
   "- `--trigger marker|pc`, `--model hybrid` only.",
   "- No cycle figure: the checkpoints perturb the RTL `mcycle`, so",
   "  `window_cycles` is suppressed. Re-run without `--cosim` to measure.",
   "- The haltreq checkpoint bottoms out at the halt slack (~a handful of",
   "  instructions). For the exact single instruction, lock-step (Mode 1) is",
   "  instruction-exact via `dcsr.step`.")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
md("---",
   "## Which mode?",
   "",
   "| | Mode 1: lock-step | Mode 2: ROI cosim |",
   "|---|---|---|",
   "| Command | `run --model cycle --cosim` | `run --model hybrid --cosim [--cosim-refine]` |",
   "| Program | small, self-initializing testbench | any, with an ROI |",
   "| Starts at | reset (or `--pc-start`) | the ROI entry (after QEMU fast-forward) |",
   "| Resolution | **exact instruction** (`dcsr.step`, zero slack) | down to the halt slack (~handful) |",
   "| Traps | compared (`mepc`/`mcause`) | ROI assumed trap-free |",
   "| Speed | slow (few records/s) | QEMU-fast to the ROI, then bounded RTL |",
   "",
   "Rule of thumb: a generator-produced unit test -> **Mode 1**. A bug deep in a",
   "real workload -> fast-forward with **Mode 2**, `--cosim-refine` to localize,",
   "then optionally reproduce the tail as a Mode-1 testbench for the exact insn.")

